{
  "_comment": [
    "Measured locally with `bazel --nohome_rc test --config=embedded",
    "//cmd/bd:bd_embedded_test --local_test_jobs=8` alongside the storage-tier",
    "and conformance targets below (all four run in the same invocation, the",
    "same way bazel.yml's bazel-embedded tier runs its shards concurrently on",
    "one host) -- race, `-test.parallel=4`, tag filter `embedded`, run with the",
    "real committed 40-shard manifest (.github/scripts/embedded-cmd-test-shards.txt)",
    "so every one of the 242 TestEmbedded* functions that existed at capture time",
    "ran exactly once (local sandboxed execution only; no remote executor or",
    "cache flags were configured for this measurement run).",
    "",
    "Each value is that top-level test's own <testcase time=...> from Bazel's",
    "generated test.xml, NOT the enclosing <testsuite time=...>. For this Go test",
    "binary / Bazel version, <testsuite time> was found empirically to be a",
    "wall-clock-since-binary-start timestamp (it does not isolate a concurrently",
    "-run top-level test's own duration under -test.parallel=4), whereas",
    "<testcase time> matched the test binary's own `--- PASS: TestX (Ys)` line",
    "exactly. Do not switch this capture to <testsuite time> without",
    "re-verifying that relationship for the toolchain in use at the time.",
    "",
    "F1 review correction (S1): an earlier pass of this file explained four",
    "outliers (TestEmbeddedUpdateConcurrent, TestEmbeddedCloseConcurrent,",
    "TestEmbeddedInitA, TestEmbeddedEpicCloseEligibleReason) as a",
    "\"queueing-delay\" artifact of Go's t.Parallel() clock starting before a",
    "test's parallel slot is granted, and shipped corrected-down weights on",
    "that theory. That explanation was WRONG and has been retracted: Go's",
    "testing package (testing.go's (*T).Parallel) adds the elapsed time to",
    "t.duration BEFORE blocking on the parallel-slot barrier, so queued-for-a-",
    "slot wait time is never counted in a test's own reported duration in the",
    "first place. The original large numbers were genuine CPU-bound running",
    "time under real resource contention (dozens of Bazel shards running",
    "concurrently on one host, each internally up to -test.parallel=4) -- this",
    "capture re-measures every test under exactly that condition (all 54",
    "cmd+storage+conformance shards running together, not solo) instead of",
    "mixing solo-measured corrections into a contended-capture baseline.",
    "",
    "Two of those four outliers (TestEmbeddedUpdateConcurrent,",
    "TestEmbeddedCloseConcurrent) are synthetic many-worker concurrency stress",
    "tests whose cost is dominated by serialized `bd` subprocess invocations",
    "behind the embedded engine's single-writer lock, not by -test.parallel",
    "contention; their recorded values below are post-fix estimates (measured",
    "value x 0.4) after cutting issuesPerWorker from 5 to 2 in both tests (see",
    "their doc comments in update_embedded_test.go / close_embedded_test.go) --",
    "pending a fresh capture to confirm. TestEmbeddedEpicCloseEligibleReason",
    "was split into TestEmbeddedEpicCloseEligibleReasonFlag (3 subtests) and",
    "TestEmbeddedEpicCloseEligibleReasonOutput (2 subtests); their recorded",
    "values are the measured combined total apportioned 3:2 by subtest count,",
    "also pending a fresh capture. TestEmbeddedInitA needed no further action:",
    "at ~196s under this consistent methodology it is close to but under the",
    "~200s single-test isolation threshold.",
    "",
    "Every test measuring at or above ~200s under this consistent load is",
    "pinned alone on its own shard in the generated manifest below (see that",
    "file's header); LPT bin-packing does this automatically as long as the",
    "weight is accurate, since no combination of lighter tests sums close to",
    "a ~200s+ single item without the packer preferring to isolate it.",
    "",
    "`seconds_per_init_fallback` is the weighted average seconds-per-init over",
    "every measured test in this file (sum of all durations / sum of all inits,",
    "where inits is discover_inits_cost()'s t.Run( count proxy), used only for a",
    "brand-new test with no entry yet (see",
    "scripts/ci/gen_embedded_cmd_shard_manifest.py's discover_inits_cost()).",
    "",
    "As with the proxied tier's duration file, these are a relative weight for",
    "LPT bin-packing, not an absolute SLA: within-shard -test.parallel=4",
    "overlap, farm noisy-neighbor effects, and future code changes all mean a",
    "shard's total packed cost is a planning estimate, not a guarantee."
  ],
  "seconds_per_init_fallback": 19.4828,
